# Root-cause protocol

1. Read the error and search relevant GitHub issues/PRs for matching symptoms.
   Run `py -3 tools/deferred_log.py status` before a fix and respect existing scope.
2. Identify the cause; fix it in the owning module, not in an app entry point.
3. Run appropriate regression checks and report fresh evidence truthfully.
4. Record the cause, fix, and verification in the issue or PR description.
5. If work remains out of scope, open/update the existing GitHub deferred issue.
6. Update an operating rule only when the failure exposes a reusable gap.
7. Commit, push, and deliver the PR under the normal delivery workflow.

Do not hide exceptions, substitute a workaround for a known root cause, or claim
verification without running it. Retired ledgers are not part of this workflow.
